WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:03.654
- [Voiceover] Until about
1902, legal food preservatives

00:00:03.654 --> 00:00:06.331
included chemicals like formaldehyde,

00:00:06.331 --> 00:00:08.922
borax and copper sulfate.

00:00:08.922 --> 00:00:12.133
That is until one guy
organized a Poison Supper Club

00:00:12.133 --> 00:00:15.800
to stop it and became
the father of the FDA.

00:00:17.491 --> 00:00:19.424
OK, here's the story.

00:00:19.424 --> 00:00:21.275
In order to keep food looking fresh,

00:00:21.275 --> 00:00:24.359
food manufacturers used
a slew of chemicals.

00:00:24.359 --> 00:00:26.647
Copper sulfate, a common pesticide,

00:00:26.647 --> 00:00:29.081
made canned peas bright green.

00:00:29.081 --> 00:00:31.919
Borax and formaldehyde
were packed with meat

00:00:31.919 --> 00:00:34.639
to make it appear fresher.

00:00:34.639 --> 00:00:36.079
At this time in our history,

00:00:36.079 --> 00:00:38.435
there were no true food regulations.

00:00:38.435 --> 00:00:40.736
You didn't need to label your ingredients.

00:00:40.736 --> 00:00:44.467
There was no safety
testing, no monitoring.

00:00:44.467 --> 00:00:48.876
Cue Dr. Harvey W. Wiley, a
chemist with the crazy idea

00:00:48.876 --> 00:00:52.096
that these chemicals had
no place in our food.

00:00:52.096 --> 00:00:54.404
He started some hygienic lab trials

00:00:54.404 --> 00:00:56.445
where he could officially test the effects

00:00:56.445 --> 00:00:58.807
of these poisons on the body.

00:00:58.807 --> 00:01:00.847
It was easy to get the chemicals,

00:01:00.847 --> 00:01:03.120
but he needed the bodies.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:06.639
And that's where the Poison Squad came in.

00:01:06.639 --> 00:01:08.770
The first 12 members of the Poison Squad

00:01:08.770 --> 00:01:11.887
were volunteers from the
Department of Agriculture

00:01:11.887 --> 00:01:15.296
and they volunteered to eat his
poisoned food for six months

00:01:15.296 --> 00:01:18.609
so he could track the
effects it had on them.

00:01:18.609 --> 00:01:20.376
Each day, the menus would change

00:01:20.376 --> 00:01:22.894
and Wiley's volunteers
never knew which poison

00:01:22.894 --> 00:01:24.561
they were consuming.

00:01:25.563 --> 00:01:29.253
A dinner at the Poison Supper
Club might look like this.

00:01:29.253 --> 00:01:31.766
Applesauce, soup, turkey,
canned stringed beans,

00:01:31.766 --> 00:01:33.532
sweet potatoes, white
potatoes, chipped beef,

00:01:33.532 --> 00:01:35.922
bread and butter, coffee, rice pudding

00:01:35.922 --> 00:01:37.505
and a little borax.

00:01:39.505 --> 00:01:42.869
Throughout the trials, Wiley
noted signs of acute poisoning

00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:45.627
including upset stomachs,
nausea, diarrhea,

00:01:45.627 --> 00:01:48.403
vomiting, kidney damage, you know,

00:01:48.403 --> 00:01:50.947
things that happen when you get poisoned.

00:01:50.947 --> 00:01:52.824
And this did not stay hidden.

00:01:52.824 --> 00:01:55.114
The press caught on and in 1906,

00:01:55.114 --> 00:01:58.184
the first food regulations were passed.

00:01:58.184 --> 00:02:01.196
This ultimately led to
the creation of the FDA.

00:02:01.196 --> 00:02:02.905
So thanks, Dr. Wiley.

00:02:02.905 --> 00:02:07.072
Our food is so much better
without all that borax.

